From 1d6630bd1ba05ef08b2e5ad75aac6c32cd321e79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:44:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [TSReader] Return the frame of a seek first, and find HEVC
 and MPEG-2 key frames

The session aligns the other streams to the PTS of the sample after a
video seek. With video and audio, the demuxer can emit audio after the
PES of the key frame before the key frame, so the session aligned to
the audio time. The reader now keeps the samples of other streams that
come before the frame of the seek, and returns them after that frame.
With video, a landing on a segment start waits for the first video
frame. While a live seek waits for the next segment, the reader reports
the PTS of the frame of the seek.

The HEVC and MPEG-2 parsers did not mark key frames, so a seek in these
streams went to the segment start. IRAP pictures and I pictures are now
key frames.

The HEVC parser read the last NAL unit of the stream before the end of
the data when a PES without data followed, and then skipped the end
completion. The end of the data now completes the frame.

A PES header can start in one segment and end in the next segment. The
PTS of the header now belongs to the segment where the PES starts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
